## Requirements

* The Rust toolchain -- install with [rustup](https://rustup.rs)
* No crates are referenced, so everything works offline

## Use

```sh
cargo build                     # debug build
cargo build --release           # release build (LTO + stripped)
cargo test                      # unit tests (src/lib.rs) + integration tests (tests/)
cargo run                       # run the CLI
cargo run -- 1 2 3              # pass numbers to add
cargo clippy --all-targets      # lints, if you have clippy
```

MakeMaker can drive these too:

```sh
makemaker build .
makemaker test .
```

## Layout

```
{{ slug }}/
├── Cargo.toml          lib + bin, both named '{{ identifier }}'
├── src/
│   ├── lib.rs          framework-free logic + unit tests
│   └── main.rs         CLI entry point
└── tests/
    └── greeter.rs      integration tests against the public API
```

## Notes

The crate is split into a library and a binary with the same name, which is the
usual Rust shape: `src/lib.rs` holds logic that `cargo test` exercises
directly, and `src/main.rs` stays a thin CLI shell over it.
